{% comment %}
  Half vertical — 400x480. Width is the constraint here, not height: the panel
  is as tall as the full view, so all six rows still fit. What has to go is the
  LO/HI column. The end dot stays: it is positioned HTML, not an svg <circle>,
  so the viewBox squashing x by ~0.55 cannot turn it into an ellipse (see
  shared.liquid).
{% endcomment %}

<style>
  {% comment %}
    Every pair is exactly XXX -> XXX, so the first column's width is fixed and
    predictable: ~92px at 14px bold. Declared at 96px rather than letting the
    text overflow a narrower track into the gap.
  {% endcomment %}
  .fx--halfv .fx-row,
  .fx--halfv .fx-head { grid-template-columns: 96px minmax(70px, auto) 58px 1fr; gap: 8px; }
  .fx--halfv { --fx-top-pad: 10px; }
  {% comment %} Row padding is py--4 (16px) on the row: 17px would not step. {% endcomment %}
  .fx--halfv .fx-pair { font-size: 14px; }
  .fx--halfv .fx-rate { font-size: 16px; }
  .fx--halfv .fx-chg  { font-size: 11px; }
  .fx--halfv .fx-dot  { r: 3px; }
  {% comment %} TREND is the last column here, so keep the dot's overhang inside it. {% endcomment %}
  .fx--halfv .fx-spark { padding-right: 3px; }
  .fx--halfv .fx-head { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
  {% comment %} Narrow plot, so a squatter shape than the wide views. {% endcomment %}
  {% comment %} Capped too: this column is narrow, so an unbounded height goes square. {% endcomment %}
  {% comment %}
    The cap, not the height calc, is what binds on OG (30px at /16 against a
    31.7px calc). /15 lets the calc win there, so the six rows fill the panel
    as they did before the row padding moved to the framework's 16px step,
    while still holding the plot to 52px on TRMNL X.
  {% endcomment %}
  .fx--halfv .fx-spark svg { height: calc((var(--screen-h) - 82px - var(--fx-top-pad)) / 6 - 33px);
                             max-height: calc(var(--screen-h) / 15); }
  {% comment %}
    Portrait: the cap above guards against the column widening in landscape
    on a big panel, but in portrait this column is as narrow as on OG and the
    panel is twice as tall, so the cap left the lower third empty. The plain
    height calc (123px in 390px, ~3:1) is the right shape here.
  {% endcomment %}
  .screen--portrait .fx--halfv .fx-spark svg { max-height: none; }
</style>

<div class="layout layout--col layout--justify-start">
  {% if fx_failed %}
    <div class="fx-error flex flex--col flex--center-y text--center">
      <span class="title">Rates unavailable</span>
    </div>
  {% else %}
    <div class="fx-list flex flex--col gap--none fx--halfv">
      <div class="fx-head grid">
        <span>PAIR</span><span class="text--right">LATEST</span><span class="text--right">CHANGE</span><span class="text--center">{% if range_label %}{{ range_label }} {% endif %}TREND</span>
      </div>

      {% for row in rows limit: 6 %}
        <div class="fx-row grid py--4">
          <div class="fx-pair">{{ row.from }}<span class="fx-arrow px--0.5">&rarr;</span>{{ row.to }}</div>
            <div class="fx-rate text--right">{{ row.rate_str }}</div>
          <div class="fx-chg flex flex--right gap--none"><span class="fx-pill inline-block rounded--xsmall py--1 px--1{% if row.change_pct < 0 %} fx-pill--down bg--black text--white{% endif %}">{{ row.change_str }}%</span></div>
          {% assign fx_end = row.points | split: " " | last | split: "," %}
          {% assign fx_end_y = fx_end[1] | times: 100.0 | divided_by: 30 %}
          <div class="fx-spark flex gap--none">
            <svg class="fx-plot block" width="100%" height="24">
              <svg class="block" viewBox="0 0 200 30" width="100%" height="100%" preserveAspectRatio="none">
                <polyline points="{{ row.points }}" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/>
              </svg>
              <circle class="fx-dot" cx="100%" cy="{{ fx_end_y }}%"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>

<div class="title_bar">
  {{ fx_icon }}
  <span class="title">Exchange Rates{% if env %} ({{ env | upcase }}){% endif %}</span>
  <span class="instance">{% if fx_failed %}No data{% else %}<span class="fx-dates text--default">{{ fx_dates }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
</div>
